# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — wiki home

This is the landing page for the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** wiki.

## Start here

- **What lives where**: [_MAP.md](./_MAP.md), the short map the agent always loads; the full entry list is `_INDEX.md`, one level up beside `wiki/`
- **Project scope**: [README.md](./README.md)
- **How the system works**: the user guide, [`../how-to/llm-wiki/user-guide.md`](../how-to/llm-wiki/user-guide.md)

## Quick reference

| Command | When |
|---|---|
| `/wiki-search "<query>"` | Look something up |
| `/wiki-update <url>` | Add one external source now |
| `/wiki-cycle` | The research cycle: gather, triage, ingest, lint, report |
| `/wrap-up` | End of a session: journal, resume files, durable entries |
| `/wiki-promote --review` | Approve entries staged in `_inbox/proposed/` |
| `/task-list` | The project's task list |

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit `_MAP.md` or the `_INDEX.md` files — they're auto-generated
- Don't move staged entries into `wiki/` by hand — `/wiki-promote` does it
- Don't suppress contradictions — both-sides-stay: keep contradictory entries cross-linked

## Concept gaps

When you notice a project, person, framework, or paper that should be tracked but doesn't have an entry yet, add it to `concept-gaps-things-mentioned-not-yet-covered.md` in this folder, so discovery can look for it (`/wiki-discover --gaps`).

(That file doesn't exist yet — create it the first time you have a gap to track. Format: one row per gap with the term, where it was mentioned, and a priority.)
